course: dictionary
lesson: 11272
title: Wriggling and wriggling out of
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wriggling means twisting and turning your body with quick, small movements. A worm has no legs, so it wriggles through the soil. «A lizard leaves its wriggling tail behind for the cat» tells you the tail is moving fast from side to side.
explain: The word has a second meaning, too. «Wriggling out of» something means trying to avoid it or escape from it. A child who wriggles in her seat when bored is moving her body, but a child who wriggles out of tidying up is trying to get away from the job. Look at the rest of the sentence to see which meaning fits.
explain: Look for clues around the word. In «a hidden zoo appears: wriggling, spinning, tiny creatures», the microscope and the word tiny tell you that wriggling means moving in quick, small twists. Put your meaning into the sentence: does twisting and turning still make sense? If yes, you have the right meaning.
fact: «Wriggling» means twisting and turning your body with quick, small movements.
fact: «Wriggle out of» means trying to avoid doing something or to escape from a difficult situation.
fact: Worms, maggots and fish move by wriggling.
fact: «Wriggling free» means twisting until you get loose.
fact: Wriggle is a verb (wriggle, wriggles, wriggled, wriggling), and wriggling can also be an adjective, as in a wriggling worm.
exercise: «Put a drop of pond water under the microscope and a hidden zoo appears: wriggling, spinning, tiny creatures.» What does wriggling mean here? | *Twisting and turning with quick, small movements | Shining brightly | Sleeping quietly | Lying perfectly still
exercise: Sam tries to wriggle out of washing the dishes. What is he trying to do? | Finish the job quickly | *Avoid doing the job | Break the plates | Ask for more dishes to wash
exercise: «A lizard leaves its wriggling tail behind for the cat.» Find and copy the word that tells you the tail is moving. | *wriggling | behind | leaves | tail
test: «A puppy wriggles out of someone's arms.» What does wriggles out of mean? | Falls asleep happily | *Twists free to escape | Hides under the bed | Barks loudly at the door
test: In the pond water, what moves by wriggling? | The microscope | A chair | *Tiny creatures | A stone
exam: Tom says wriggling only describes worms. What does the sentence «a lizard leaves its wriggling tail behind» show? | Lizards have no tails | Only worms can wriggle | *Wriggling can describe any body part moving with quick twists, not only worms | Tails cannot move
